  "description": "The formal requirements for a Calvin University BSN include successful completion of 120 semester hours, completion of the designated program of study and the designated Core, and a minimum grade point average of 2.0 both overall and in the program of concentration. Pre-nursing Curriculum Prior to beginning the BSN program, students must complete nine courses, obtaining a combined minimum GPA of 2.8 (in addition to an overall minimum GPA of 2.8). Students must earn a minimum grade of a C in each course, including any corequisite labs. A course may be repeated only once, a course may be withdrawn from only once, and no more than two courses may be repeated. Courses taken at another institution and transferred must have a grade of at least a B.",
